<p data-line="69" class="code-line">In the previous article I wrote "when in doubt, go Apache 2.0," and that hasn't changed. Since both Qwen3.6 and Gemma 4 are Apache 2.0, they're the easy-to-choose top two from a commercial use perspective. Note that the flagship Qwen3.6-Max has non-public weights and is API-only; what's openly available is the mid-range tier like 27B / 35B-A3B.</p>
<h3 id="japanese-language-performance" data-line="71" class="code-line"><a class="header-anchor-link" href="#japanese-language-performance" aria-hidden="true"></a> Japanese Language Performance</h3>
<p data-line="73" class="code-line">I'll also update the Japanese language performance evaluation. This is based on Nejumi Leaderboard 4 (July 2026 edition) combined with my own hands-on impressions.</p>
<table data-line="75" class="code-line">
